    <string name="investment_assumptions">Offline planning estimate using equal monthly periods, not actual-day bank accrual. Dates are anchored to the original day and clamped at month ends. Taxes, fees, penalties and missed deposits are excluded. Currency is a denomination, not an exchange conversion.</string>

    <string name="investment_sip_assumptions">Investments occur at the beginning of each period. Monthly return is the stated annual percentage divided by 12. Step-up increases the previous monthly contribution after each selected interval, rounded to currency precision. Returns are estimates and are not guaranteed.</string>

    <string name="investment_rd_assumptions">Quarterly compounding uses the equivalent monthly growth factor (1 + annual rate / 400)^(1/3). Every deposit is made at the beginning of its monthly period. Fractional-quarter values are estimates.</string>

    <string name="investment_fd_assumptions">Cumulative deposits compound completed periods and earn proportional simple interest for any final partial period. Periodic deposits pay interest on unchanged principal without reinvestment. Periodic annual yield assumes hypothetical reinvestment at the same rate; actual payouts are not reinvested.</string>

    <string name="investment_amount_error">Use a positive amount below 1 trillion within currency precision.</string>

    <string name="investment_rate_error">Use an annual rate from 0 to 100, with up to four decimal places.</string>

    <string name="investment_sip_rate_error">Use a return from −99.99 to 100, with up to four decimal places.</string>

    <string name="investment_tenure_error">Use 1–600 whole months. Years must convert exactly to months.</string>

    <string name="investment_step_error">Step-up cannot be negative. Percentage must be 0–100; amounts must fit currency precision and remain below 1 trillion.</string>

    <string name="investment_overflow_error">This projection exceeds the supported total of 1 quintillion. Reduce the amount, return, step-up or duration.</string>

